  [US-01-AC01] The system stores a name, an address and a phone number for every customer.
  [US-01-AC02] The system accepts a customer record that has no bank account.
  [US-01-AC03] A customer has at most one bank account.
  [US-01-AC04] Given a customer record that lacks a name, an address or a phone number, When the record is saved, Then the system rejects the record.
  [US-02-AC01] The system stores a name, a description, a price and an image for every product.
  [US-02-AC02] Given a product record that lacks a name, a description, a price or an image, When the record is saved, Then the system rejects the record.
  [US-02-AC03] The price of a product is stored as a decimal number.
  [US-02-AC04] A product may be referred to by any number of order items, including none, and a product exists independently of the order items that refer to it.
  [US-03-AC01] Given a known customer and at least one order item that refers to an existing product, When the order is submitted with a payment method, Then the system registers an order with the submission date as its order date and the status submitted.
  [US-03-AC02] Each order item records a quantity, a unit price and exactly one product, and belongs to exactly one order.
  [US-03-AC03] Each order belongs to exactly one customer, and a customer may have any number of orders.
  [US-03-AC04] The unit price of an order item is stored as a decimal number.
  [US-03-AC05] The payment method recorded on an order is one of bank, card or cash.
  [US-03-AC06] An order item exists only as part of the order it belongs to, and cannot be moved to another order; when an order is removed from the system, its order items are removed with it.
  [US-04-AC01] Given a customer who is not known to the system, When an order is submitted for that customer, Then the system rejects the submission and registers no order.
  [US-04-AC02] Given an order submission that contains no order item, When the order is submitted, Then the system rejects the submission and registers no order.
  [US-04-AC03] Given an order item that refers to a product that does not exist, When the order is submitted, Then the system rejects the submission and registers no order.
  [US-05-AC01] Given an order with one or more order items, When the order is registered, Then the system records a total amount for the order.
  [US-05-AC02] The total amount of an order equals the sum over its order items of quantity multiplied by unit price.
  [US-05-AC03] The total amount of an order is stored as a decimal number.
  [US-06-AC01] Given an order with the status submitted, When OrderStaff receives the order, Then the system sets its status to pending.
  [US-06-AC02] Given an order whose status is not submitted, When OrderStaff attempts to receive the order, Then the system rejects the request and leaves the status unchanged.
  [US-06-AC03] The status of an order is always one of submitted, pending, filled, shipped or closed.
  [US-06-AC04] The status of an order changes only from submitted to pending, from pending to filled or to closed, from filled to shipped, and from shipped to closed.
  [US-07-AC01] Given an order with the status pending, When OrderStaff marks the order as filled, Then the system sets its status to filled.
  [US-07-AC02] Given an order whose status is not pending, When OrderStaff attempts to mark the order as filled, Then the system rejects the request and leaves the status unchanged.
  [US-07-AC03] A filled order can next be set only to shipped.
  [US-08-AC01] Given an order with the status pending, When OrderStaff declines the order, Then the system sets its status to closed.
  [US-08-AC02] Given an order whose status is not pending, When OrderStaff attempts to decline the order, Then the system rejects the request and leaves the status unchanged.
  [US-08-AC03] Given a declined order, When an invoice is requested for the order, Then the system rejects the request.
  [US-09-AC01] Given an order with the status filled, When OrderStaff marks the order as shipped, Then the system sets its status to shipped.
  [US-09-AC02] Given an order whose status is not filled, When OrderStaff attempts to mark the order as shipped, Then the system rejects the request and leaves the status unchanged.
  [US-09-AC03] Given an order that is marked as shipped, When the system records the change, Then the status of its invoice and of any payment against that invoice remains unchanged.
  [US-10-AC01] Given an order whose status is filled or shipped and that has no invoice, When the Accountant issues an invoice for the order, Then the system records an invoice with a date, a decimal amount, a payment method and the status issued.
  [US-10-AC02] Given an order that already has an invoice, When the Accountant attempts to issue another invoice for the order, Then the system rejects the request.
  [US-10-AC03] Given an order whose status is submitted, pending or closed, When the Accountant attempts to issue an invoice for the order, Then the system rejects the request.
  [US-10-AC04] An order has at most one invoice, and every invoice belongs to exactly one order.
  [US-10-AC05] The status of an invoice is always either issued or paid.
  [US-10-AC06] Once an order has been filled, invoicing and shipping proceed independently of each other: issuing an invoice does not require the order to have been shipped, and marking the order as shipped does not require an invoice to have been issued, so the two may happen in either order or at the same time.
  [US-11-AC01] Given an invoice with the status issued, When the Customer submits a payment against the invoice with a date, an amount and a payment method, Then the system records the payment with the status pending.
  [US-11-AC02] Every payment method recorded for an order, an invoice or a payment is one of bank, card or cash.
  [US-11-AC03] The amount of a payment is stored as a decimal number.
  [US-11-AC04] The status of a payment is always one of pending, completed or failed.
  [US-11-AC05] Given an invoice with the status paid, When the Customer attempts to submit a further payment against the invoice, Then the system rejects the request.
  [US-11-AC06] Every payment settles exactly one invoice, and a payment is recorded against an invoice rather than directly against an order.
  [US-12-AC01] Given an invoice whose most recent payment has the status failed, When the Customer submits a new payment against the invoice, Then the system records a separate payment with the status pending.
  [US-12-AC02] A failed payment keeps the status failed when a new payment is submitted against the same invoice.
  [US-12-AC03] An invoice may have any number of payments.
  [US-13-AC01] Given a payment with the status pending, When the Accountant confirms the payment, Then the system sets the status of the payment to completed.
  [US-13-AC02] Given a pending payment against an issued invoice, When the Accountant confirms the payment, Then the system sets the status of the invoice to paid.
  [US-13-AC03] Given a payment whose status is completed or failed, When the Accountant attempts to confirm the payment, Then the system rejects the request and leaves the status unchanged.
  [US-13-AC04] The status of an invoice changes only from issued to paid.
  [US-13-AC05] Confirming a payment does not change the status of the order billed by the invoice.
  [US-14-AC01] Given a payment with the status pending, When the Accountant rejects the payment, Then the system sets the status of the payment to failed.
  [US-14-AC02] Given a payment with the status pending, When the Accountant rejects the payment, Then the status of its invoice and of its order remain unchanged.
  [US-14-AC03] Given a payment whose status is completed or failed, When the Accountant attempts to reject the payment, Then the system rejects the request and leaves the status unchanged.
  [US-14-AC04] The status of a payment changes only from pending to completed or from pending to failed.
  [US-15-AC01] Given an order with the status shipped whose invoice has the status paid, When OrderStaff closes the order, Then the system sets its status to closed.
  [US-15-AC02] Given an order with the status shipped whose invoice does not have the status paid, When OrderStaff attempts to close the order, Then the system rejects the request and leaves the status unchanged.
  [US-15-AC03] Given an order whose invoice has the status paid but whose status is not shipped, When OrderStaff attempts to close the order, Then the system rejects the request and leaves the status unchanged.
  [US-15-AC04] The status of a closed order cannot be changed.
  [US-15-AC05] A filled order is closed only after both the shipping of the order and the settlement of its invoice have completed, whichever of the two finishes last.
